;; Negative fixture: primed generic head with space inside <...> — must lex-error (unclosed
;; bracket, not CommaInKeywordBody). Arc 109 "the comma dies in the reader" retired the
;; comma-carrying multi-param spelling this fixture originally used (`<i64, i64>`) — a comma
;; inside `<...>` is now its OWN unconditional lex error, so a comma-bearing body would trip THAT
;; arm before ever reaching the whitespace check this test is about. A single-param bracket with
;; a trailing space (`<i64 >`) still exercises the exact same `UnclosedBracketInKeyword` arm
;; without depending on the retired comma — the axis under test is PRIMED-vs-UNPRIMED parity
;; (see the sibling `_unprimed_space` fixture), not param count.
(:wat::core::defn :user::take [m <- :wat::core::HashMap'<wat::core::i64 >] -> :wat::core::nil nil)
